WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:03.170
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

00:05.170 --> 00:06.460
Oh, by the way.

00:06.460 --> 00:10.290
What are you going to do when I quit
this part-time job after summer break is over?

00:10.580 --> 00:13.920
I'm going to hire. Actually, I've already
put out a recruitment about hiring.

00:14.580 --> 00:16.830
Speaking of, there is a poster at the entrance.

00:17.000 --> 00:21.710
Yeah. So, Sajo-kun, when the kouhai comes,
you'll become a senpai too, you know?

00:21.960 --> 00:23.170
Well, I guess so.

00:23.170 --> 00:25.130
What's with that ho-hum reply!?

00:26.250 --> 00:28.130
Well, take care of the rest of this as well.

00:28.130 --> 00:29.500
Aye aye, sir.

00:31.630 --> 00:34.210
"Reiji Kawashima"... Is that here?

00:35.130 --> 00:36.420
U-um...

00:36.420 --> 00:37.710
Oh, yes?

00:43.500 --> 00:46.420
Huh? I've felt this vibe somewhere before...

00:50.750 --> 00:52.130
Ichinose-san!?

00:52.130 --> 00:53.880
Um, do you need something?

00:54.250 --> 00:56.380
I saw the recruitment sign on the entrance and...

00:56.380 --> 00:57.040
Okay.

00:57.500 --> 00:59.210
What!? For the part-time job!?

01:01.250 --> 01:02.710
Is she going to be okay...?

01:17.000 --> 01:20.960
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

01:17.000 --> 01:20.960
<b>is a Realist</b>

01:21.080 --> 01:26.670
Nozoki dasu sora no gourei de omoi kakaeta mama shuppatsu

01:26.670 --> 01:31.380
Me wa au noni kaze de yurete toomawari

01:32.460 --> 01:37.920
Akogare matataki no shutter omoide wa kokoro kazatta

01:37.920 --> 01:43.330
Kono jikan, suki mitai modokashii noni

01:44.420 --> 01:49.290
Hanarete chikazuite akirame kaketa yume

01:49.540 --> 01:54.960
Umaku oritateru hi oikakete mitaina

01:54.960 --> 02:00.380
Joukuu ippai ni natta tsutae kirenai koto

02:00.540 --> 02:06.170
Nazeka iro chigai no kimi no honne surechigatta

02:06.170 --> 02:14.460
Mayotchai sou dakedo sora wa zutto futatsu no kodou

02:14.460 --> 02:16.960
Nando mo tsutaeta

02:17.130 --> 02:23.130
Ao no kanjou kuttsuke tara donna keshiki hirogaru no kana

02:23.130 --> 02:27.830
Irodotta omoi shiritainda

02:34.670 --> 02:36.960
Oh yeah! That's Mina-chan!

02:34.830 --> 02:37.750
<b>Aren't You Way Too Guilty?</b>

02:36.960 --> 02:38.960
Huh? Do you know her?

02:39.130 --> 02:41.170
She's a fine young lady who's a regular.

02:41.330 --> 02:44.460
Aw! Seriously!? Mina-chan, huh!?

02:44.670 --> 02:46.540
I'm a lucky one!

02:46.790 --> 02:50.000
The old guy becomes younger when he gets psyched up.

02:50.540 --> 02:51.460
<b>Mina Ichinose</b>

02:54.710 --> 02:56.250
Mina-chan, you're hired!

02:56.250 --> 02:56.920
Oh!

02:57.170 --> 02:59.670
Hang on! Isn't that too premature, after all?

02:59.960 --> 03:02.460
Well, I know who Mina-chan is.

03:02.460 --> 03:03.250
Okay...

03:03.460 --> 03:04.750
U-um...

03:04.960 --> 03:08.250
My wife will be pleased too. Follow me, Mina-chan.

03:10.380 --> 03:13.210
Well, with this I can quit without reserve.

03:13.210 --> 03:16.210
So, it was you, Mina-chan. It's just that...

03:16.290 --> 03:20.170
Well, those bangs, you see...
Can something be done about them?

03:20.250 --> 03:23.250
Oh? That's a rather harsh thing to say.

03:23.420 --> 03:25.330
Well, I also agree, but...

03:24.000 --> 03:26.670
You know, I am pleased that you came, but...

03:26.960 --> 03:29.670
I know! Shall I cut them for you?

03:29.790 --> 03:30.420
What!?

03:30.580 --> 03:31.210
Huh!?

03:33.750 --> 03:36.040
Wait a sec! Ma'am, please stop!

03:36.250 --> 03:40.250
Oh, hi. I was explaining about the part-time job just now.

03:40.250 --> 03:41.670
Is that so?

03:42.170 --> 03:44.710
Even though she likes to look after others,
anyone would panic over that.

03:44.710 --> 03:46.540
In any case, what should I do about this?

03:46.880 --> 03:51.290
If my relationship with Ichinose-san is only through
this part-time job, then this is where I should...

03:51.790 --> 03:53.580
Nice to meet you, my name is Sajo.

03:54.000 --> 03:54.670
What...?

03:55.040 --> 03:59.250
I heard from the owner, that Ichinose-san,
you are quite the book lover or something like that?

03:59.250 --> 04:00.330
Y-yes...

04:00.630 --> 04:03.250
When you read books, don't your bangs get in the way?

04:03.790 --> 04:05.540
What do you usually do with them?

04:05.750 --> 04:07.830
Oh! U-usually, I...

04:11.420 --> 04:12.790
I-it's like this...

04:13.420 --> 04:15.580
This is the first time I've seen Ichinose-san's face...

04:16.210 --> 04:18.960
That's fine! Well then, let's go with that.

04:18.960 --> 04:19.920
Y-yes!

04:19.920 --> 04:22.540
Then I look forward to working
with you starting from tomorrow.

04:22.830 --> 04:24.830
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

04:25.830 --> 04:27.420
Good mornin'...

04:27.790 --> 04:28.500
Huh?

04:29.080 --> 04:32.790
Hang on, since she's a kouhai for a part-time job,
isn't it better not to use formal language?

04:33.130 --> 04:34.540
Plus, she's a classmate.

04:35.040 --> 04:36.540
Morning, Ichinose-san.

04:36.540 --> 04:38.790
Oh... Good morning...

04:38.790 --> 04:40.130
Her voice is so quiet!

04:40.130 --> 04:41.500
Uh, let's see...

04:41.630 --> 04:43.750
Ichinose-san, who sits next to me...

04:43.750 --> 04:44.580
Huh?

04:44.830 --> 04:46.000
That's you, right?

04:46.290 --> 04:48.960
We haven't talked very much,
but I'm looking forward to working with you.

04:52.380 --> 04:53.380
Yeah...

04:53.500 --> 04:57.580
Her replies are slow! Are we going
to be able to get along if it's like this...?

04:58.080 --> 05:00.210
Oh! You've come, Sajo-kun!

05:00.420 --> 05:03.000
Good morning. You're full of energy.

05:03.210 --> 05:06.330
As you're a senpai starting from today,
I'm leaving Mina-chan in your care.

05:07.210 --> 05:08.250
I'll do my best.

05:08.250 --> 05:15.670
Besides any heavy labor, show Mina-chan the job.
Take extra care not to form any wicked thoughts.

05:15.880 --> 05:17.250
What are you saying!?

05:17.250 --> 05:18.880
I'm kidding!

05:22.040 --> 05:23.670
<b>Ichinose</b>

05:22.130 --> 05:23.790
First off is, the bangs...

05:28.290 --> 05:30.920
That's right. When you're doing
your part-time job, use that style, okay?

05:32.000 --> 05:33.080
Well then, shall we get going?

05:33.460 --> 05:37.380
First thing is to look at the list of the books that got
sold yesterday, while organizing the shelves, okay?

05:37.380 --> 05:38.750
It's super easy.

05:39.790 --> 05:45.750
Uh, it's fine to just nod when it's me, but make sure
to properly answer when it's a customer, okay?

05:46.290 --> 05:47.540
Y-yes!

05:49.750 --> 05:51.290
When I look at it like this...

05:51.790 --> 05:53.540
There's surprisingly a lot of things to do...

05:53.540 --> 05:55.330
U-um!

05:55.330 --> 05:56.080
Huh?

05:56.630 --> 05:59.250
Oh, I'd have you use a stepladder there, but...

05:59.460 --> 06:00.670
Let's not have you do that.

06:01.380 --> 06:03.580
I-I can do this much!

06:03.710 --> 06:07.080
You say that, but if you stumble,
are you okay that I'll be one who'll catch you?

06:07.330 --> 06:09.920
Th-that's... No way...

06:09.920 --> 06:10.580
Oof!

06:12.290 --> 06:14.000
What's left is dealing with customers.

06:14.710 --> 06:18.420
Since the store's already open,
the customers could come in at any time.

06:19.830 --> 06:23.420
For the time being, Ichinose-san, you can keep
things tidy and in order, like I just showed you.

06:23.920 --> 06:28.330
I'll do the stuff that's high up and dealing with customers,
and why don't you be near the register to observe.

06:28.750 --> 06:29.750
You'll need that too...

06:31.040 --> 06:31.960
<b>In training</b>

06:32.040 --> 06:33.540
Pass the string through and...

06:33.750 --> 06:34.580
There...

06:36.170 --> 06:38.790
Having you put it on yourself, would've been better...

06:39.250 --> 06:41.080
Her emotional personal space is not good...

06:41.790 --> 06:46.330
Uh, Ichinose-san. Is there anything
you don't understand up to this point?

06:46.630 --> 06:47.380
Um...

06:47.880 --> 06:50.670
If there's nothing in particular, then that's fine.

06:50.920 --> 06:51.500
Th...

06:51.500 --> 06:52.380
There is...?

06:52.670 --> 06:53.580
There isn't...

06:54.290 --> 06:56.250
Hey, we're not connecting well...

06:57.130 --> 07:00.960
Well then, since I've generally shown you
the work duties, the rest is just to get used to things.

07:04.710 --> 07:07.210
You'll eventually start to get it, but...

07:07.500 --> 07:09.710
There are a lot of customers who are just browsing.

07:10.290 --> 07:13.210
Ichinose-san, shall we have you look at
the placements of the buttons on the register?

07:13.420 --> 07:14.130
Yes...

07:18.750 --> 07:19.420
Huh?

07:20.540 --> 07:21.210
Uh, um...

07:21.500 --> 07:22.830
Hang on, you're actually buying!?

07:21.630 --> 07:23.130
<b>Great Writers</b>

07:21.630 --> 07:23.130
<b>of Japan</b>

07:23.290 --> 07:28.290
The fact that you don't have "Yukio Mishima"
is a disgrace to secondhand bookstores...

07:28.790 --> 07:32.170
The masterpiece that expresses
the sweetness of sexuality; "The Music"!

07:32.170 --> 07:34.960
He changed an unforgivable sexual act
into a beautiful artistic creation,

07:34.960 --> 07:39.670
and to have a place call itself a secondhand bookstore
without his presence is outrageous!

07:38.080 --> 07:40.210
What the hell is this old man talking about...?

07:40.580 --> 07:41.460
Hey there.

07:41.750 --> 07:43.210
So, it'll be these two items, right...?

07:43.380 --> 07:44.040
Huh?

07:44.460 --> 07:49.420
I totally don't get what he's saying, but it's clear
he brought merchandise up to the register.

07:49.420 --> 07:51.460
Would you like us to put book covers on these?

07:51.750 --> 07:53.040
Would you please?

07:53.380 --> 07:57.330
Okay. For the two books, that'll be 220 yen.

07:58.170 --> 07:59.710
<b>Great Writers of Japan</b>

08:02.880 --> 08:03.920
Thank ya!

08:07.920 --> 08:11.330
For that kind of customer, as long as you don't let
your guard down, then things will work out.

08:11.580 --> 08:12.210
Huh?

08:13.630 --> 08:14.710
Ichinose-san...?

08:16.290 --> 08:16.960
What!?

08:18.830 --> 08:20.420
Let's head to the back for the moment, okay!?

08:21.630 --> 08:22.500
Excuse me!

08:22.500 --> 08:24.250
I'd like to ask for your wife!

08:24.420 --> 08:25.460
What's happened?

08:25.460 --> 08:29.670
Ichinose-san encountered an idiosyncratic customer,
and she ended up crying!

08:29.960 --> 08:32.130
What!? And Mina-chan?

08:32.130 --> 08:36.170
I'm having her rest in the back room.
But sir, please don't go there.

08:36.540 --> 08:39.380
I think a woman is suited for this kind of thing.

08:39.380 --> 08:41.630
Oh! Okay, got it...

08:42.040 --> 08:42.960
Thanks.

08:43.290 --> 08:44.790
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

08:45.040 --> 08:48.830
Can Ichinose-san be entrusted
to do this by herself once I quit...?

08:49.710 --> 08:50.580
Or rather...

08:50.790 --> 08:53.130
<b>Monthly Magazine</b>

08:50.790 --> 08:53.130
<b>Mutant</b>

08:51.000 --> 08:54.420
First of all, there's even trouble forming
in the communications between employees,

08:54.420 --> 08:56.380
let alone dealing with customers, you know...?

08:55.210 --> 08:56.790
<b>Special Issue</b>

08:55.210 --> 08:56.790
<b>Catman</b>

08:57.000 --> 09:01.500
Maybe I'll discuss this with the old guy.
Plus, it's possible he might have a good idea.

09:02.420 --> 09:03.630
Um, sir?

09:03.630 --> 09:04.290
Yeah?

09:04.710 --> 09:06.000
For this part-time job,

09:06.000 --> 09:10.580
it's crucial to a certain degree, to have the skill
to deal with customers like that person, right...?

09:10.580 --> 09:12.130
Yeah, I think so...

09:12.500 --> 09:15.630
I don't think Ichinose-san is cut out for this, so...

09:15.630 --> 09:19.210
What!? Sajo-kun, are you basing that,
just off her appearance...?

09:19.210 --> 09:21.460
In that case, sir, are you going to look after her?

09:22.130 --> 09:25.710
And if you say something like, "I'll do
all the things that Ichinose-san can't do,"

09:25.960 --> 09:27.790
your wife isn't going to keep quiet about that!

09:27.790 --> 09:28.580
Oh...

09:28.790 --> 09:30.040
Oh, I'm sorry...

09:30.580 --> 09:34.000
Apparently, I'm more irritated
about Ichinose-san than I thought.

09:34.460 --> 09:38.210
Whether it's incompatibility of temperament,
or it's just I'm narrow-minded, or...

09:38.500 --> 09:39.710
Mina-chan is...

09:39.710 --> 09:40.330
Huh?

09:41.040 --> 09:44.790
Mina-chan is this store's cute regular...

09:45.290 --> 09:45.920
Huh!?

09:46.250 --> 09:49.290
What happened to your usual energetic spirit, old guy!?

09:49.500 --> 09:50.960
C'mon me, think...!

09:52.250 --> 09:54.750
At school, she's always alone and...

09:56.040 --> 10:00.580
But at the least, this used bookstore
and the old guy who cares about her,

10:01.210 --> 10:04.040
for Ichinose-san, is where she feels she belongs, right...?

10:04.830 --> 10:08.920
Um... I'll try to talk to Ichinose-san a little, okay?

10:08.920 --> 10:10.210
R-really?

10:10.210 --> 10:13.580
Yes... But please don't expect too much.

10:14.000 --> 10:15.670
Yeah, got it...

10:17.130 --> 10:20.460
Something like her ending up hating
this place just can't happen.

10:20.880 --> 10:22.380
For the old guy's sake too...

10:23.460 --> 10:27.130
In that case, I should be the one to say something, since
it's not going to matter what happens to me after this.

10:25.380 --> 10:29.000
As a woman, on occasion, it is fine to be dominant.

10:29.670 --> 10:31.420
Ma'am, thank you very much.

10:31.710 --> 10:32.710
No problem.

10:33.130 --> 10:36.790
I was just explaining to Mina-chan
about the mental attitude for work.

10:37.250 --> 10:39.000
Please leave the rest to me.

10:39.580 --> 10:42.500
Ma'am, weren't you in the middle
of finalizing the account book?

10:42.500 --> 10:44.210
Yes, that's right.

10:44.580 --> 10:46.170
Well then, I'll see you later.

10:53.500 --> 10:56.540
Ichinose-san... Would you mind listening to me?

10:57.000 --> 10:59.960
That customer from earlier was
a weird person, wasn't he?

11:01.330 --> 11:04.710
You're not going to be able to deal with customers
the way you'd like to, from the get-go.

11:05.330 --> 11:07.500
It may also be unavoidable that
you end up crying because you're scared.

11:08.540 --> 11:12.500
For that kind of customer, it's effective
to talk to them in sort of a frivolous tone.

11:13.000 --> 11:17.040
If you let them think that you can't understand
difficult words, then they shut up.

11:17.880 --> 11:20.130
If it was you, Ichinose-san, then for example,

11:20.130 --> 11:23.380
if you'd said things in a valley girl kind of way,
he might've become intimidated.

11:23.710 --> 11:27.580
You see, dealing with customers is difficult after all,
and there's no right answer.

11:27.960 --> 11:29.500
But there are wrong answers.

11:29.710 --> 11:34.210
No matter how troublesome it may seem, if
it's a customer, then you can't respond in the wrong way.

11:35.420 --> 11:38.380
So, Ichinose-san, can you do that?

11:38.380 --> 11:39.210
Huh?

11:39.540 --> 11:42.000
Even though normally you may
not be good at talking clear and crisply,

11:42.330 --> 11:45.790
can you show that you're a "capable person,"
when you're at this part-time job?

11:49.920 --> 11:51.750
If you can't do that, then you're not cut out for this!

11:52.170 --> 11:54.790
You gotta make do with the allowance
you get from your parents.

11:53.040 --> 11:54.790
Idiot! Calm down!

11:54.790 --> 11:58.540
As a senpai, what I shouldn't be
doing is taking away her options.

11:55.670 --> 11:58.540
You shouldn't have to go so far as
to force yourself to do a part-time job.

11:58.540 --> 11:59.750
It's to let her choose!

12:01.210 --> 12:03.540
My bad... Just this is enough.

12:03.830 --> 12:07.290
Can you just tell me if you're willing
to deal with customers?

12:09.040 --> 12:13.210
Honestly, this make me think that
it would be better if she just quits at this rate.

12:14.080 --> 12:18.920
To have Ichinose-san come as a customer
and for the old guy to devotedly talk to her,

12:18.920 --> 12:22.750
isn't that just about right for both
Ichinose-san and the old guy...?

12:23.250 --> 12:24.250
Don't want to...

12:24.250 --> 12:24.880
Huh?

12:25.420 --> 12:28.290
I don't want to! I don't want to quit!

12:28.670 --> 12:30.080
Huh? Why?

12:30.580 --> 12:35.170
I-I will make it work, so that I can do this!
So please, don't make me quit!

12:35.170 --> 12:37.380
Hang on! Please lift your head up! Seriously!?

12:37.540 --> 12:44.040
You know, I-I'm just a part-time worker!
Ichinose-san, I can't make you quit or anything like that!

12:44.040 --> 12:48.040
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

12:44.040 --> 12:48.040
<b>is a Realist</b>

12:49.170 --> 12:51.580
I will make sure I can do anything, so please...!

12:51.880 --> 12:54.580
I got it! I got it, so please lift your head up!

12:57.330 --> 12:58.630
Uh-huh! Uh-huh!

13:01.380 --> 13:02.750
What's happened!?

13:02.750 --> 13:05.170
Sir! Ichinose-san will stay on!

13:05.170 --> 13:05.880
What!?

13:05.880 --> 13:07.830
Let's do our best starting from tomorrow! Okay!?

13:08.290 --> 13:12.670
I see... It's already this time of hour,
so the two of you can wrap up for today.

13:12.670 --> 13:13.330
Huh!?

13:13.750 --> 13:17.420
Oh, but the daily work probably
hasn't been finished, so I'll stay.

13:17.420 --> 13:21.170
No, it's fine. More importantly,
you'll come again tomorrow for sure, right?

13:21.540 --> 13:23.080
Very well...

13:23.460 --> 13:26.170
Well then... Shall we go home, Ichinose-san?

13:26.170 --> 13:27.500
Y-yes!

13:27.920 --> 13:29.920
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

13:29.920 --> 13:32.960
<b>We buy</b>

13:29.920 --> 13:32.960
<b>used books.</b>

13:34.460 --> 13:36.040
I'm the worst...

13:42.830 --> 13:50.580
<b>Morals &</b>

13:42.830 --> 13:50.580
<b>Discipline</b>

13:43.250 --> 13:45.790
What's wrong, Ichinose? You look down.

13:46.040 --> 13:50.580
I'm sorry... I haven't been getting along
with my younger sister recently, and...

13:50.580 --> 13:52.580
<b>Mina</b>

13:50.580 --> 13:52.580
<b>Today</b>

13:50.590 --> 13:52.580
<b>No response.</b>

13:53.080 --> 13:55.040
It'll be fine, okay?

13:55.040 --> 13:56.080
Yuri-chan...

14:01.460 --> 14:04.080
<b>Sajo, Aika, K</b>

14:01.460 --> 14:04.080
<b>Sajotchi's ignoring us.</b>

14:01.460 --> 14:04.080
<b>Aika</b>

14:01.460 --> 14:04.080
<b>Part-time job?</b>

14:01.460 --> 14:04.080
<b>Yeah.</b>

14:04.500 --> 14:05.250
Crap...

14:05.830 --> 14:07.330
<b>Sajo, Aika, K</b>

14:05.830 --> 14:07.330
<b>These 2 are participating</b>

14:05.840 --> 14:07.330
<b>in a video chat.</b>

14:07.540 --> 14:09.210
Why is it a video chat?

14:10.040 --> 14:10.880
Here!

14:10.880 --> 14:12.750
I absolutely want to go, you know!?

14:13.080 --> 14:15.250
Huh, the inside of the store is stylish too.

14:15.250 --> 14:21.250
Isn't it? Let's take lots of photos! Plus, once
school starts, things will get busy again anyway.

14:21.630 --> 14:24.830
That's fine, but... Kei,
did you finish the summer homework?

14:25.080 --> 14:27.540
Huh? I've been seriously doing
club activities, you know?

14:27.540 --> 14:31.710
That's what I thought. Well then, this'll be
a reward after you finish the homework.

14:31.960 --> 14:33.750
I'll explain any parts that you don't understand.

14:33.920 --> 14:36.000
Aichi, I seriously love you!

14:36.000 --> 14:36.960
Jeez!

14:36.960 --> 14:37.630
Oh!

14:38.000 --> 14:40.000
<b>Sajo</b>

14:38.000 --> 14:40.000
<b>I finished my part-time job and conked out.</b>

14:38.130 --> 14:40.000
You know, when one is being a girl...

14:40.380 --> 14:42.500
Occasionally, you gotta take in some calories, right?

14:42.630 --> 14:45.880
Yeah! It looks like you can customize to low-fat too...

14:46.170 --> 14:48.460
Huh!? Are you listening?

14:48.750 --> 14:50.830
But the toppings absolutely...

14:50.830 --> 14:53.670
Oh! It looks like Sajotchi was at his part-time job after all!

14:53.670 --> 14:55.420
I-is that so...?

14:55.830 --> 14:58.670
Yeah. When I sent that he should
join us right away, it says it got "read."

14:58.670 --> 15:00.710
What!? H-hang on, wait a sec!

15:02.830 --> 15:04.040
Sajotchi!

15:04.040 --> 15:05.630
It's been a while since we talked!

15:06.000 --> 15:08.960
Hey! Oh, is Natsukawa not on video?

15:08.960 --> 15:11.000
By the way, are you like tired or something?

15:11.250 --> 15:13.080
Even I have a lot of things going on...

15:13.080 --> 15:15.500
Is that so? Spill it! Spill your guts!

15:15.790 --> 15:18.290
Okay then... So, I need some advice.

15:18.630 --> 15:21.710
Today, at my part-time job,
I made a girl bow down on the ground and...

15:21.710 --> 15:22.540
What!?

15:22.880 --> 15:24.080
Aren't you way too guilty!?

15:24.080 --> 15:26.000
Um, let's pretend you didn't hear that...

15:26.290 --> 15:27.250
No can do!
That's impossible!<b></b>

15:27.630 --> 15:28.750
What did you do?

15:28.750 --> 15:33.250
Um... Well, she's a shy person and
consequently this was a tragedy that occurred,

15:33.250 --> 15:35.960
because I didn't consider her personality, so to speak...

15:35.960 --> 15:38.170
In other words, Sajotchi, you were at fault?

15:38.170 --> 15:38.830
Well...

15:39.080 --> 15:40.460
How do I put this...?

15:41.210 --> 15:45.580
T-talk to us. Well, you can to us, you know...?

15:47.210 --> 15:48.170
Actually...

15:52.380 --> 15:57.130
So, that's my concern, or rather...
It's like, "what should I do, starting from tomorrow?"

15:57.540 --> 16:00.210
I wonder if that girl will come tomorrow...

16:00.210 --> 16:01.330
I bet that she won't come.

16:01.330 --> 16:03.500
Ugh! Just kill me now!

16:03.500 --> 16:05.750
S-Sajotchi, cheer up!

16:05.880 --> 16:08.250
You know, you're not the only one who was at fault.

16:08.250 --> 16:08.790
Huh?

16:09.420 --> 16:12.580
In the first place, if that girl had been
able to properly communicate,

16:12.580 --> 16:14.670
then that kind of thing wouldn't have happened.

16:15.290 --> 16:18.670
As a senpai at her part-time job,
you tried to light a fire under her, right?

16:18.960 --> 16:21.170
Well... I guess that's true...

16:21.500 --> 16:24.290
You had a proper reason, so...

16:24.750 --> 16:25.500
Right...

16:25.500 --> 16:26.130
Yeah...

16:26.710 --> 16:28.380
I said I got it!

16:28.880 --> 16:31.920
Sorry! I'm being told to go take a bath! See ya!

16:31.920 --> 16:32.670
What!?

16:32.670 --> 16:34.710
Hey! That was sudden!

16:37.670 --> 16:41.500
Hang on. By any chance,
was that encouragement just now?

16:41.710 --> 16:43.500
What!? Why would I say something like...?

16:43.790 --> 16:46.750
Well, it was an objective opinion, so to speak, so...

16:46.750 --> 16:47.920
It's just your imagination!

16:48.250 --> 16:49.130
S-sorry...

16:50.500 --> 16:52.960
Leaving that aside, Natsukawa,
how are you doing lately?

16:53.380 --> 16:54.750
How am I doing? As in what...?

16:54.750 --> 16:58.080
Well, since summer break started,
we haven't seen each other in a while, so...

16:58.420 --> 17:00.380
Wh-when you put it that way, I guess that's true...

17:01.630 --> 17:04.540
Well, if you're having fun hanging out
with Ashida, then I'm glad.

17:05.380 --> 17:08.540
Oh... By the way, Natsukawa,
why do you have your video turned off?

17:08.790 --> 17:10.630
I'd just gotten out of the bath, so...

17:10.630 --> 17:11.920
What!? Oh, sorry!

17:11.920 --> 17:14.830
Hey... About that chat from earlier...

17:14.830 --> 17:15.750
Y-yeah?

17:16.290 --> 17:19.170
Make sure you listen properly
to what that girl has to say, okay?

17:19.380 --> 17:20.670
I got it. Thank you!

17:25.920 --> 17:27.670
<b>We buy</b>

17:25.920 --> 17:27.670
<b>used books.</b>

17:29.000 --> 17:30.460
Good mornin'...

17:34.920 --> 17:36.790
<b>Ichinose</b>

17:35.040 --> 17:36.790
Morning, Ichinose-san.

17:36.790 --> 17:38.960
Y-yes! Good morning!

17:39.670 --> 17:42.000
So... I'm seriously sorry about yesterday...

17:42.000 --> 17:43.250
O-okay...

17:43.500 --> 17:47.540
There's still time before the store opens,
so shall we leisurely do some organizing?

17:47.880 --> 17:49.290
Y... Yes!

17:49.880 --> 17:52.330
Oh? That's a better reply compared to yesterday.

17:53.170 --> 17:55.250
Does she have a reason why
she can't quit or something...?

17:56.500 --> 17:59.710
It's store opening time, huh?
Alright, I'll go flip the sign out front.

18:00.210 --> 18:01.960
Oh! Uh, I can...!

18:01.960 --> 18:03.500
Okay then, I'll leave that to you.

18:03.790 --> 18:04.540
Yeah!

18:08.920 --> 18:10.290
I-it's done!

18:10.630 --> 18:12.080
Well done.

18:12.830 --> 18:13.580
Huh!?

18:13.580 --> 18:17.380
Oh! Yeah, there's dust floating in the air!

18:17.380 --> 18:21.170
That was close! You know, there's like times
when she kind of looks like a little kid...

18:22.170 --> 18:23.380
Welcome!

18:24.330 --> 18:25.830
I... I will do it!

18:25.830 --> 18:26.540
Okay...

18:26.920 --> 18:27.750
What!?

18:27.750 --> 18:28.920
<b>In training</b>

18:35.040 --> 18:37.580
The type of customer who silently places
merchandise at the register, huh?

18:38.040 --> 18:40.130
This might be tough for Ichinose-san...

18:40.500 --> 18:46.880
W-welcome. Th-that will be... One item for 130 yen.

18:46.880 --> 18:47.500
Oh?

18:47.500 --> 18:49.000
O-out of 500 yen...

18:49.000 --> 18:54.830
Um... Your change is 370 yen.

18:55.000 --> 18:55.630
Oh!?

18:55.630 --> 18:56.380
Oh, let's see...

18:56.380 --> 19:01.250
Hello! For this size, we can put a book cover on it,
but what would you like to do?

19:03.000 --> 19:03.920
Thank ya!

19:06.540 --> 19:09.790
What's happened to you, Ichinose-san!?
You're totally different from yesterday!

19:10.330 --> 19:12.210
I'm saying that's amazing! What did you do!?

19:12.500 --> 19:15.540
Oh... I looked at stuff like videos
on dealing with customers and...

19:15.750 --> 19:18.830
That's commendable, you know!? Let's keep
this up to continue dealing with customers!

19:18.830 --> 19:23.920
O-okay. Um, for the time being, I'll go organize
just the stuff in the back...

19:29.210 --> 19:33.080
Looking at her today as well,
it really doesn't seem like she wants to quit, so...

19:33.710 --> 19:36.580
Even while I wouldn't poke my nose
into a family's circumstances,

19:36.880 --> 19:39.790
what is the reason why Ichinose-san
doesn't want to quit...?

19:40.830 --> 19:44.080
Sajo-kun, Mina-chan, it's about time for a break.

19:44.080 --> 19:44.920
Okay.

19:49.290 --> 19:53.460
Isn't the timing now or never,
to make small talk with Ichinose-san?

19:53.670 --> 19:56.670
Oh, Ichinose-san. You came today.

19:56.670 --> 19:57.330
What?

19:57.710 --> 20:00.790
What the hell am I saying!?
That totally sounds like sarcasm!

20:01.960 --> 20:04.460
There was no way I could quit, so...

20:05.000 --> 20:09.630
Huh... In the first place, Ichinose-san,
why were you thinking of doing a part-time job?

20:11.750 --> 20:13.960
Because I want to become "independent."

20:14.380 --> 20:19.170
What!? Isn't that like amazing!? You know,
I've never even thought about something like that.

20:19.170 --> 20:19.830
Yeah...

20:20.210 --> 20:23.290
But isn't that too soon?
We're still 1st-years in high school, you know?

20:23.750 --> 20:25.960
I want to detach myself from my older brother, so...

20:26.250 --> 20:29.080
Huh... Ichinose-san, so you have a big brother.

20:29.460 --> 20:31.170
He's a Morals & Discipline Committee Member 3rd-year...

20:31.170 --> 20:33.880
What? A male Morals & Discipline Committee Member?

20:34.080 --> 20:36.670
<b>Morals &</b>

20:34.080 --> 20:36.670
<b>Discipline</b>

20:34.540 --> 20:36.460
That teddy bear-like senpai, huh?

20:37.290 --> 20:40.500
She doesn't look like him.
Everything from the sense of size to...

20:41.080 --> 20:43.540
But why? You should be affectionate and spoiled by him.

20:44.670 --> 20:47.790
Oh. Even if you want to be affectionate, you can't?

20:48.210 --> 20:48.960
Uh-huh.

20:49.830 --> 20:53.080
Or rather, this is already becoming
a chat about family issues, isn't it...?

20:53.630 --> 20:58.330
I don't think we know each other well enough
to talk to that extent, so I should stop around here...

20:58.790 --> 21:01.960
You see, I love my big brother...

21:02.250 --> 21:02.830
Huh!?

21:03.330 --> 21:05.670
When I read books at home, I always...

21:06.710 --> 21:12.330
I sit in between my big brother's legs,
and I use his stomach as a back rest and read.

21:12.880 --> 21:15.380
It's warm and comfy and...

21:16.670 --> 21:19.420
What's up with that!? You can totally relax...!

21:19.920 --> 21:24.250
But one time, my big brother brought a woman over...

21:24.580 --> 21:28.750
From then on, the time I had to talk
to my big brother started decreasing and...

21:29.380 --> 21:32.250
Still, I wanted to be with my big brother and...

21:29.540 --> 21:32.250
What!? Is this a topic that I should be hearing about!?

21:32.250 --> 21:34.750
Isn't this a matter that shouldn't be discussed with me!?

21:32.670 --> 21:36.330
One day, I decided that I would tell
my big brother about my feelings...

21:34.750 --> 21:37.290
Wait a sec! I'm getting a bad feeling!

21:37.710 --> 21:40.580
I don't want to hear this... But I want to hear it...!

21:41.040 --> 21:44.920
When I got home from school,
there were shoes there, other than my family's...

21:45.540 --> 21:49.750
And they were... I realized immediately
that those were Yuri-san's.

21:50.290 --> 21:53.790
But at that time, I couldn't care less,
what people would say about me and...

21:54.420 --> 21:56.000
I headed to my big brother's room and...

21:56.000 --> 21:58.210
I didn't even knock, and I opened the door!

21:59.170 --> 22:00.210
And then...!

22:00.540 --> 22:01.670
"And then"...!?

22:02.040 --> 22:03.420
A-and then...!

22:03.880 --> 22:09.460
And then, Yu... Yuri-san was hunched
over my big brother and...!

22:09.750 --> 22:11.040
She was kissing him...!

22:28.580 --> 22:31.040
Mou, shitsukoi! Danante, ne

22:31.330 --> 22:34.630
Aa. Iwanakya yokatta na...

22:35.460 --> 22:41.580
Demo ne nande sona kyuu ni sokkenai kao shite kuruno...

22:43.290 --> 22:45.500
Kidoku no mama oitekebori na message

22:45.500 --> 22:47.790
Demo group dato henshin aru mitai na

22:48.000 --> 22:49.960
Chikai to omottara tooku natte

22:50.210 --> 22:51.750
Nande konna sabishin daro

22:51.750 --> 22:53.630
Kyou wa oikakete... kurenai no?

22:53.630 --> 22:55.170
Sunao ni naretara ii noni

22:56.630 --> 23:02.960
Datte hajimete shitta no konna setsunai kimochi ga aru kototte...

23:02.960 --> 23:04.380
Nanoni, nee!

23:04.380 --> 23:05.920
Doushite itchau no??

23:05.920 --> 23:07.670
Nande naisho nano!?

23:07.880 --> 23:10.040
Modokashii darake de...

23:10.040 --> 23:11.420
Aa! Aa!

23:11.420 --> 23:13.130
Ienai yo konna no

23:13.130 --> 23:17.130
Dakedo sakki wa honne janai kara

23:17.130 --> 23:18.500
Tsutawatte yo

23:18.580 --> 23:20.210
Doushite okotchau no...

23:20.210 --> 23:21.750
Kawaiku dekinai no...

23:21.750 --> 23:24.210
Kirai ni natta no...??

23:24.380 --> 23:27.080
Aa! Aa! A, aa!

23:29.080 --> 23:30.040
Doushite

23:30.710 --> 23:32.000
Kirai ni naranai de

23:35.040 --> 23:36.420
...Kiite, "Anone...!"
